  "original_external_pr_body": "Follow-up for the unresolved review threads of merged pull requests\n#30, #12 and #3, and for the review of this pull request.\n\nWindows shell screen (Cmd dialect):\n\n- #30: a for header with no do cleared the loop. FOR /F with a command\n  source cleared the loop. Both fixed here; a set that starts with\n  %FILES% is pinned as Review.\n- A bare for with no header no longer opens a pending loop, and the\n  body delimiter is the first do after the loop set closes, so\n  `cmd /c echo ready for review` screens Clear.\n\nPOSIX wrapper parsing:\n\n- `env` skips a lone `-` in every position, as GNU env does, so a\n  refused executable after other options is blocked, not cleared.\n- `command` accepts grouped lookup switches (`command -pv git`).\n- Quoted `${@}`, `${@:n}` and `${!prefix@}` expand to one word per\n  element and stay under review in env assignments and find operands.\n\nRead-only classification:\n\n- `fd` recognizes attached filter values (`fd -tf`, `--type=f`) as\n  data, so plain file searches are read-only while an attached filter\n  followed by an execution action stays mutable.\n\nAlready fixed or carried, no change here: #12 `shell_screen.ml:1240`\n(#30 commit 346ea2c), #3 `test_cli.ml:134` (open #26).\n\nThis branch also contains the head of open #20.\n\nEvidence: each new verdict row fails before its fix and passes after.\n`dune build @fmt`, `dune build --profile release` and\n`dune runtest --profile release` pass (221 tests).\n\nSee also: #30, #12, #3\n",
